# Code owners for the Dhruv monorepo.
#
# Solo-maintainer repo: one owner for everything. The per-path rows below are
# not redundancy — they are the list of areas where a review is *load-bearing*
# rather than routine, and they become meaningful the moment a second
# maintainer exists (change the owner on that row, nothing else).
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS only auto-requests review; it only *blocks* a merge when a
# ruleset sets `require_code_owner_review`, which needs GitHub Pro on a private
# repo (see scripts/env/apply-branch-protection.ps1). Until then this file is
# documentation + auto-assignment.

# Default owner for everything.
*                                   @saikumarkalli

# --- Areas where a change is expensive to get wrong -------------------------

# Platform contracts and the decision register. Nothing here is "just docs":
# DECISIONS.md is append-only and PLATFORM.md is the source of truth.
/platform/                          @saikumarkalli
/platform/DECISIONS.md              @saikumarkalli
/platform/contracts/                @saikumarkalli

# CI/CD, release signing, and the cost budgets in ADR-0026.
/.github/workflows/                 @saikumarkalli
/scripts/ci/                        @saikumarkalli
/scripts/env/                       @saikumarkalli

# Database. Migrations are append-only executed history (ADR-0032); the
# declarative schema files must stay equivalent to them.
/supabase/                          @saikumarkalli

# Shared library — every app depends on it, so a break here breaks everything.
/libs/core/                         @saikumarkalli

# Compliance surfaces (DPDP): consent, erasure, privacy policy.
/PRIVACY.md                         @saikumarkalli
/SECURITY.md                        @saikumarkalli